# Cross-device correctness (hard requirements)

These are checkable requirements, not guidelines. A change that fails any rule is not done.

## Layout

- Never use `vh` for full-height sections. Use `dvh` or `svh` (see `styles/tokens.css` and `RESPONSIVE.md`). Mobile browser chrome makes `vh` wrong.
- Never use `100vw`. It includes the scrollbar and causes horizontal overflow. Use `100%` or `dvw`.
- No element may cause horizontal page scroll at any width from 320px up.
- Every new layout uses flex or grid with `gap`. No fixed pixel widths on containers.
- Prefer `clamp()`, `min()`, `max()`, grid `auto-fit` / `minmax()`, and `aspect-ratio` over adding new breakpoints.
- Media queries are **mobile-first** (`min-width` only). Do not add `max-width` layout queries.
- Breakpoints (tokens only): `--bp-sm` 640, `--bp-md` 1024, `--bp-lg` 1280. In `@media`, use those pixel values with a token comment — `var(--bp-*)` is not reliable inside media queries.
- New breakpoints must come from `--bp-*` in `styles/tokens.css`.

## Touch and input

- Every interactive element has a minimum 44×44px hit area on touch devices.
- Any hover-triggered behavior MUST have a touch equivalent. Detect with `(hover: none)` and `(pointer: coarse)` — never user-agent sniffing. A feature that only works on hover is a bug, not a desktop feature.
- Form inputs are never smaller than 16px font size (smaller triggers iOS zoom).

## Media

- Every `img` and `video` carries explicit dimensions or `aspect-ratio` to prevent layout shift.
- Video is `muted` + `playsinline` wherever it autoplays, or iOS will refuse to play it.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, `navigator.connection.saveData`, and `effectiveType` of `slow-2g` / `2g` by falling back to poster images with no video loading.

## Safe areas

- Fixed and sticky elements pad with `env(safe-area-inset-*)`. The viewport meta includes `viewport-fit=cover`.

## Process (required after every HTML / CSS / JS change)

- After ANY change to HTML, CSS, or JS, re-verify the affected area at **320px**, **375px**, **768px**, **1024px**, and **1440px** before reporting the work as done.
- State in your response which viewports you checked and what you observed. If you did not check, say so explicitly.
- If a change works on desktop but not on touch, it is not finished.
- Run `npm run lint:responsive` and `npm run check` before treating layout work as done. See `RESPONSIVE.md`.
- Never introduce a framework, bundler, or dependency into this project. It is hand-built static HTML/CSS/JS and stays that way. (Dev-only npm tooling for lint/check is allowed.)
